[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If I could use one word to describe the launch of the P1 and the P1 Max, I would use the word disastrous. The P1 launching, even launching as a Kickstarter for one thing, was simply a bad call by any cubic. What was intended as a pre-order campaign came across as'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'one of the leading brands in resin unintentionally making themselves look like a startup, which just rire of desperation. And with an add-on front and center on all of their marketing, which was just, well, yeah, we\'ll get to'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it. Coupled with the initial ignorance of several glaring hardware issues that they initially said they would not be changing until the community said, okay, then we\'re not buying it then. But now, these have been resolved. And we'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actually have a pretty decent machine now available. And then the P1 Max. Honestly, one of my favorite printers I have ever used. And what big mistake did they make with that one at launch? Well,'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'they didn\'t actually launch it on launch day. And they didn\'t even tell me until about an hour before my video was due to go live, at which point, considering it was the middle of the night, I was'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'asleep. But now, and I\'m saying this, I bloody hope this time it\'s true or I\'m going to look like an absolute dick again, it\'s actually coming out. So, let\'s consider this video as an update to both those previous reviews because'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'any cubic now offer a solid contender printer and a very desirable printer in the P1 Max. And this video is basically they asked me to remind you these exist. So, consider them. Hi, I\'m Ross and this'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is Fammer Videos. And yeah, this video is sponsored by Any Cubic. I don\'t care. I\'ve already done the reviews. You can go and watch them. There\'s some updates in here, but yeah, why not? Why not at this point? Put your comment and carry'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on. As always, they\'ve got zero say as to what I put into this video. All they care about is getting the word out. So, believe me or don\'t on that. At this point, I\'m beyond defending it. If you\'re new here, I\'d recommend maybe'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'listen to my fair warnings about the machine before making that call. But yeah, let\'s recap on the P1. This is a decent printer. It\'s certainly a step up from what any cubic have delivered before. again, except for the M3'

[02:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Premium, which in its time was amazing. But this is the closest they\'ve been since with some more modern tech built in, which you could take as gimmicks in some cases, but pressure sensing specifically is helpful. I think it'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'looks nice. It\'s easy to set up, and for your traditional style of 3D printer where it\'s open to all materials, but you do need to dial in the settings yourself, unless you use any Cubix resin where they\'ve got some profiles in'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'place, though, honestly, I\'d still dial it in myself. This is probably the best we\'ve seen yet. So, let\'s talk about the issues because that\'s what we need to cover. First was the lid. Now, as I noted in my review, the opacity of the'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lid was so poor that I actually had resin cure on the top of my build plate. Now, I am in a windowless room, so this wasn\'t sunlight. It was clearly due to my studio lights. Now, yes, in fairness, I have stronger lights than probably 99%'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of home users because I use them for filming. But still, this is the worst result I\'d ever seen in terms of indoor lights curing resin through a lid. Now, despite me raising this with Any Cubic'

[03:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'before that review went live and them telling me they\'re not changing it, I\'ve got to offer kudos to the community for telling them off for this because they did change it during the Kickstarter campaign to a much darker lid. They'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'didn\'t put that on the updates or announcements page. They just replied to a few comments. Well done, Any Cubic. Really good on that one. Another issue I pointed out was the max fill line in the resin bat. Now, thankfully, this was just a printing error, and the bat'

[03:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'should now be marked to hold a full liter of resin without any risk of overspill. And there\'s also the wavy layer on top of the LCD, which reduces peel forces. Now, as noted, this does have an impact on print quality, but as'

[03:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I hope I was clear in my earlier video, it\'s not by a huge amount. It\'s hardly even noticeable at all. I actually did a direct comparison of this to the same 14K panel on the M7, which has the same screen, but doesn\'t have that wavy'

[04:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'layer. [music] And the only difference that is clear is that there\'s an extra line gap or two filled in at the bottom left on my exposure test I normally print. That got filled in on the P1. So, I\'m sure we agree this is absolutely'

[04:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'minimal for miniatures and the like. I\'ve said many times once you enable anti-aliasing and image blur, I highly doubt any of us would see a difference between this or any other modern printer of the same ilk. The most amusing'

[04:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'element of this whole product was the dual VAT and dual build plate. You can print two resins with different settings at the same time. Now, this hasn\'t changed. It still exists, and it still lacks the heating function of the'

[04:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'primary VAT, which is odd considering the main use of the dual VAT is for more professional resins. you know, the ones that would most likely benefit from consistent printing temperature. Yeah. So, look, I\'m not making these things.'

[04:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'See, I can say what I want. Like, sponsored video, it\'s agreed. I can say what I want. Yeah. Anyway, what I really wanted to cover about these is where the idea even came from. Now, this is incredibly popular in dental printing.'

[05:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In fact, most of the ad showed both gums and teeth being printed at the same time. But I think any cubic excitedly releasing this showed that they completely misunderstood why that was such a valuable add-on in the dental'

[05:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'industry, which I think is industrial-grade printers have traditionally been very, very expensive. I\'m not talking four grand expensive. I\'m talking like tens of thousands'

[05:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'expensive. So, at some point, dental techs would have probably described the issues to those brands and how long it takes to print the different models. Then, they\'ve got to print again. And I bet those industrial machines have a whole process to go through for material'

[05:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'changeover. Now even in the dental world, very few people would have had the capital to invest in one printer, never mind multiple, in order to achieve this. So the dual vat was born to save money. Everything\'s driven by money'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'really, isn\'t it? But that doesn\'t work here. Like even I said you could, let\'s say you were printing two armies of models in different colors. you just print one army in one color and one in another color and not sacrifice an'

[06:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'error. It\'s it\'s dafted. And when you\'re looking at this for an industrial application, when you can get a second printer for around $500, $600, well, compared to tens of thousands of'

[06:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'dollars, surely you just buy a second printer. But honestly, when it comes to being a professional machine, as I said in my review, the P1 still very much has the look and feel, but with some of the components being the lower grade of'

[06:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'industrial-grade hardware, it\'s just more pretense than polish. Now, that doesn\'t make it a bad machine. In fact, it\'s a very good machine. It looks decent. Solid build plate, aside from the resin sitting on top, which you can'

[06:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work around with the tray and a scraper. It\'s got a large vat. It\'s got a high enough resolution screen. It\'s open to your own settings, though. that\'s no longer a USB. And it\'s got decent pressure sensing, which should lead to'

[06:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fewer failed prints delivered as fast as possible and without any of that weird surface scarring that we typically got from ACF release film. And with directly compatible accessories for venting fumes out of your house with the Air Pure 2.0,'

[07:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even though I don\'t remember what the 1.0 was. Was that the little USB batterypowered ones? Anyway, this is a decent all-in-one package that should give you very little trouble. so long as you get a good one. Now, overall, I'

[07:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'would call this a fair product at a fair price. It\'s competitive. It\'s got some USPS and so long as any Cubic use this as a platform to improve usability, I honestly think this one currently beats'

[07:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Saturns and the GK3s on features for the price. But the real showstopper, which I think will be an absolute must-have for a lot of people, is the P1 Max. Again, I already said this in my'

[07:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'review. So, this isn\'t any cubic paid me to make a video. I\'m saying something different. Go back and watch it. But yeah, as I said, I had a review unit of this. I made my review. I published it only for them to delay it a few months.'

[08:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And in that time, what have they changed? They\'ve strengthened the back. Yeah. Basically, to help prevent Z or Z wobble, depending where you are in the world, due to all the weight of larger prints. The Z-axis has been reinforced'

[08:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with extra struts, which I can\'t even show you because they\'re behind the back panel inside the machine. Now, honestly, I didn\'t have any wobble issues in my prototype, and I don\'t fancy ripping two perfectly good printers apart just to'

[08:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'confirm what any Cubic are now telling us. But they\'re saying that\'s what they\'ve done. They\'ve made it stronger. Brilliant. That\'s just a good thing. But the genius of this machine isn\'t even in the strength. It\'s in the complete'

[08:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'package because the P1 Max has the very unique selling point for those of you like me looking for a printer to do artistic works. The screen is large, but the printer itself isn\'t particularly huge. By making that screen ratio closer'

[08:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to 4x3 rather than 16x9, they\'ve actually reduced the width in favor of more depth, so it doesn\'t take up as much horizontal real estate on a worktop, which means we get a larger print volume without taking up'

[09:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'significantly more desk space than the next nearest large machine. And this has [music] everything the P1 has with one exception, the stupid dualbat thing that nobody wanted. And seriously, if you\'re out there and you\'ve got the Dualbat, I'

[09:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'would love to hear from you. Let me know if you actually use it and find it useful. I I haven\'t heard from one person yet in any of my reviews. So, please, if you\'re out there, you might be a unicorn. But yeah, this has got the'

[09:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'same up andover dark lid, which is removable. It\'s got all the same ports, the same UI. It works with the AirPure 2.0. The build plate here is incredibly heavy. But again, I refer you back to the just leave it in place and get a'

[09:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tray and a scraper method, which is something weirdly that many of my commenters seem particularly angry about me doing. Like this process or even this plate is somehow a crime against resin printing. But this is a solid stainless'

[10:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'steel plate rather than cheap aluminium or aluminum for most of you watching. This won\'t scrape as bad. And machining these plates to have a taper seems difficult for even the best companies out there. I haven\'t seen one with a'

[10:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'steel plate and a tapered top yet. And yes, I would absolutely prefer this plate to be the same style as the Form 4, the GK2 or 3, or the Jupiter 2. But is it enough that I care? Well, no, not anymore because I now scrape all the'

[10:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'models off those plates when they\'re still mounted, too. So, I\'ve just got used to this process. I suppose the be all and end all is this is absolutely a printer worth considering. Many of you know who my favorite brand of printer'

[10:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are. And if you don\'t, just ask in the comments. I\'m not going to turn an any cubic sponsored video into an advert for someone else. But a lot of people are asking me if I\'d now choose this machine or one from that other company. And I\'ve got to be honest, I don\'t know. [music]'

[10:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s always going to be a personal choice. And I unfortunately can\'t relate on that in a lot of ways because I\'ve got the very self-aware YouTuber privilege of the brand just send them to me. So I do now use both machines for'

[11:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different jobs. But even though this does miss out on that more userfriendly workflow and the branded resin profiles are nowhere near as refined, this does something that no other printer on the'

[11:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'market even offers. Because here you can print anything from detailed miniatures with fine details to large statues in fewer print jobs. And as someone who often flits between those exact two'

[11:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'model types, I think if I could choose only one printer today, it probably would be this warts and all because with the near 4x3 aspect ratio, I\'d be less'

[11:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'likely to find a dimensional constraint on a bed no matter what I\'m printing. However, as many of us are acutely aware and we should remain vigilant, is that any cubic as a brand do not have the'

[11:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'best track record in terms of afterare service. They aren\'t the worst, but they\'re nowhere near the best. So, whilst neither of these are the absolute best machines on the market, and to be'

[12:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fair, there\'s no such thing as the best, considering different people want different things, the P1 Max is currently the only machine in the last 2 or 3 years that has actually moved the hardware in a direction I think more'

[12:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'people want. And it\'s all about that screen. Next time, do a square one, one:one screens. That\'s what we want. Now, for more info, please check out my full reviews as I said in the intro. And'

